From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] taskschd, schedsvc: folder name checks, EnableTask on an XML-disabled task, DeleteTask without a name, task XML roots

Ground truth from Wine's scheduler test: folder names with / : * ? " < > | or a . or .. part are ERROR_INVALID_NAME (GetFolder, CreateFolder, DeleteFolder); CreateFolder of nothing but backslashes is E_INVALIDARG; DeleteTask without a name acts on the folder (ERROR_DIR_NOT_EMPTY while it holds tasks); EnableTask(TRUE) enables a task whose XML says Enabled false and the state follows (cleared when the task is deleted or registered anew); a root element other than Task is SCHED_E_UNEXPECTEDNODE and a task without any action SCHED_E_MISSINGNODE. 11 todo_wine marks removed.
